Given a local ring R with an ideal I, we investigate the properties of zero submodules of local cohomology modules $\Ext^d_R(I)$, where $d$ represents the Cohen-Macaulay dimension of $R$. By examining the zero submodules of $\Ext^d_R(I)$ for various ideals $I$, we establish connections to rationally connected and strongly rationally connected properties in local rings. Notably, for a prime ideal $\mathfrak{p}$ in $R$, the condition that the zero submodule $\mathfrak{p}\Ext^d_R(I)
eq 0$ holds implicitly for all ideals $I$ with $\mathfrak{p}
otin \Ass_R R/I$. Furthermore, we connect this condition to the coherence of certain modules $\Ext^d_R(I)$, specifically when $\mathfrak{p}
otin \Ass_R R/I$, as demonstrated by the results focusing on $\Ext^d_R(X)$. Moreover, our analysis reveals the connection between zero submodules of local cohomology and strong rational connectedness in local rings.
